1
00:02:06,163 --> 00:02:12,283
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:12,858 --> 00:02:16,818
The bloodshed should stop
in Bithynia, Osman Bey.

3
00:02:17,465 --> 00:02:19,935
I want an everlasting peace.

4
00:02:20,506 --> 00:02:22,056
Can I come in my Bey?

5
00:02:22,745 --> 00:02:24,035
Come in, Boran.

6
00:02:40,421 --> 00:02:42,261
The Catalan has spoken, my Bey.

7
00:02:43,525 --> 00:02:47,415
They took orders from Michael Kosses.

8
00:03:24,623 --> 00:03:26,353
Michael Kosses.

9
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,690
Let's take a tour.

10
00:03:37,807 --> 00:03:39,237
Sure.

11
00:04:08,183 --> 00:04:10,223
You are pretty, Masha Allah (praise be)

12
00:04:11,372 --> 00:04:15,122
So, don't you have a Bey, a husband?

13
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:19,206
No.

14
00:04:21,964 --> 00:04:24,224
I haven't found someone for me yet.

15
00:04:26,014 --> 00:04:27,594
Of course you can't, girl.

16
00:04:27,901 --> 00:04:30,841
Unbelievers are useless.

17
00:04:35,245 --> 00:04:38,525
We can find you a valiant from Kayi , ha?

18
00:05:25,207 --> 00:05:27,917
You see the situation, Michael Kosses.

19
00:05:36,583 --> 00:05:39,073
They ambushed us
on our way back from Sogut.

20
00:05:41,478 --> 00:05:43,188
Some run away.

21
00:05:43,436 --> 00:05:44,836
Some fell down.

22
00:05:47,475 --> 00:05:49,565
Only this one left in our hands.

23
00:05:55,902 --> 00:05:57,972
Their aim...

24
00:05:59,468 --> 00:06:04,248
was to abduct my guest Priest Gregor.

25
00:06:09,110 --> 00:06:11,650
Is Priest Gregor with you, Osman Bey?

26
00:06:13,763 --> 00:06:15,233
I'm surprised.

27
00:06:15,782 --> 00:06:17,822
I didn't know it.

28
00:06:24,623 --> 00:06:26,053
Sir, are you fine?

29
00:06:27,548 --> 00:06:29,628
Don't worry Andreas.

30
00:06:29,951 --> 00:06:31,161
I am fine.

31
00:06:31,595 --> 00:06:34,355
Your wound must be treated
as soon as possible.

32
00:06:35,072 --> 00:06:36,952
It can't wait any longer.

33
00:06:40,868 --> 00:06:43,078
I asked him who he works for.

34
00:06:46,678 --> 00:06:48,628
Maybe you want to hear too.

35
00:06:58,407 --> 00:07:01,857
We attacked you
with the order of Lord Kosses.

36
00:07:14,901 --> 00:07:17,731
This is a cheap trick, Osman Bey.

37
00:07:20,691 --> 00:07:22,861
Apparently, someone is...

38
00:07:26,699 --> 00:07:29,439
...trying to put the blame on me.

39
00:07:33,311 --> 00:07:35,031
Look at him!

40
00:07:36,205 --> 00:07:38,365
If he was one of my men...

41
00:07:39,434 --> 00:07:41,774
he wouldn't be in this situation.

42
00:07:45,373 --> 00:07:48,113
Also I would have already
taken Priest Gregor.

43
00:07:51,873 --> 00:07:56,533
Either Rogatus or someone else
is trying to offload the blame.

44
00:07:58,218 --> 00:08:00,388
Do not let them trick you, Osman Bey.

45
00:08:05,251 --> 00:08:08,241
Only Allah cannot be tricked, Kosses.

46
00:08:12,790 --> 00:08:14,880
They may trick me.

47
00:08:16,475 --> 00:08:18,485
Don't worry about me.

48
00:08:20,658 --> 00:08:22,498
Don't, Osman Bey!

49
00:08:22,751 --> 00:08:25,791
I have just learned that you have Gregor.

50
00:08:29,487 --> 00:08:32,167
How can I have done this?

51
00:08:33,654 --> 00:08:35,914
You are a wise man, Osman Bey.

52
00:08:36,719 --> 00:08:39,839
Everyone in Bithynia tries to
trick each other.

53
00:08:40,339 --> 00:08:41,909
You know it very well.

54
00:08:44,957 --> 00:08:46,827
You are right, Kosses.

55
00:08:48,644 --> 00:08:53,194
You Lords are expert at tricking people.

56
00:08:59,383 --> 00:09:00,753
However...

57
00:09:01,827 --> 00:09:06,637
if this dog is telling the truth...

58
00:09:10,264 --> 00:09:12,864
you are going to pay for it dearly.

59
00:09:14,899 --> 00:09:17,509
If I had known that you had Gregor...

60
00:09:18,395 --> 00:09:22,345
...I would have done everything I could
so far, Osman Bey.

61
00:09:23,714 --> 00:09:28,004
They tried to trick you and me,
both of us.

62
00:09:34,963 --> 00:09:37,283
Do not let them trick you Osman Bey.

63
00:09:49,116 --> 00:09:51,286
No matter how good the hunter is...

64
00:09:53,094 --> 00:09:55,264
The wolf always finds a way out.

65
00:09:59,422 --> 00:10:04,702
I am neither prey nor a hunter,
Osman Bey.

66
00:10:08,246 --> 00:10:10,446
You should know that.

67
00:10:21,831 --> 00:10:23,681
Excuse me.

68
00:10:35,465 --> 00:10:37,775
You are excused, Kosses.

69
00:10:48,311 --> 00:10:49,931
Just for now.

70
00:10:58,007 --> 00:10:59,597
You are excused.

71
00:11:27,471 --> 00:11:29,251
Malhun Hatun.

72
00:11:29,679 --> 00:11:31,716
Mari liked Turkish rugs a lot.

73
00:11:31,716 --> 00:11:33,066
Beyond just liking them.

74
00:11:34,574 --> 00:11:37,994
I want to buy your rugs, if it's okay.

75
00:11:38,582 --> 00:11:41,462
With pleasure.
We would be glad.

76
00:11:47,530 --> 00:11:50,660
- Sir, are you okay?
- I am absolutely not!

77
00:11:51,448 --> 00:11:54,329
- We are going back right now!
- Sure.

78
00:11:55,079 --> 00:11:57,011
- Where are the horses?
- Back there, sir.

79
00:11:57,011 --> 00:11:58,141
Hurry!

80
00:12:01,103 --> 00:12:02,593
Ladies.

81
00:12:03,984 --> 00:12:06,484
I am grateful to you
for this beautiful conversation.

82
00:12:06,813 --> 00:12:10,923
Besides, I want you to know that I'm very
excited for the trade we're going to make.

83
00:12:11,719 --> 00:12:14,679
The rugs will be ready, Mari.
We'd like to see you again.

84
00:12:14,833 --> 00:12:16,733
Of course.

85
00:12:17,772 --> 00:12:20,322
I loved it here.
I'll visit again.

86
00:12:20,789 --> 00:12:24,229
You can come anytime.
Our doors are open to anyone.

87
00:12:34,890 --> 00:12:36,430
Malhun Hatun...

88
00:12:38,294 --> 00:12:42,214
I said to Mari that rugs would be ready,
but we lack rugs.

89
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:45,270
It's hard to deliver on time.

90
00:12:45,724 --> 00:12:50,394
Don't worry, Bala Hatun, there are
Kizilbeyoglu tent's rugs.

91
00:12:52,075 --> 00:12:54,445
If we still lack, we'll ask the
tents around.

92
00:12:56,875 --> 00:12:59,265
Do you think we can make it on time?

93
00:12:59,654 --> 00:13:01,104
Of course we will.

94
00:13:02,082 --> 00:13:03,532
We are one.

95
00:13:06,314 --> 00:13:07,374
You are right.

96
00:13:09,862 --> 00:13:12,242
You are good at trading.

97
00:13:13,216 --> 00:13:16,816
I think you are the one
to be responsible for this job.

98
00:13:20,358 --> 00:13:23,048
We'll manage, Inshallah.

99
00:13:25,764 --> 00:13:27,434
Thank you.

100
00:13:32,664 --> 00:13:34,784
Brother, is there a problem?

101
00:13:35,166 --> 00:13:38,016
We are leaving right now, Mari.

102
00:13:44,547 --> 00:13:45,847
Osman Bey.

103
00:13:49,994 --> 00:13:52,804
Your tent is as glamorous as you deserve.

104
00:13:53,003 --> 00:13:55,873
Your ladies took care of me very well.

105
00:13:56,276 --> 00:13:57,886
I am grateful.

106
00:13:58,321 --> 00:14:00,661
I hope your brother is grateful too.

107
00:14:04,732 --> 00:14:09,112
He has seen things that
he hasn't before.

108
00:14:36,138 --> 00:14:39,778
You let Kosses go despite what
the Catalan said, Osman Bey.

109
00:14:39,910 --> 00:14:44,560
I want to know, brother.
I want to know who is backstabbing whom.

110
00:14:49,223 --> 00:14:51,763
They wanted to bait Rogatus.

111
00:14:53,221 --> 00:14:54,891
Then Kosses.

112
00:14:56,935 --> 00:14:59,365
They are setting a game again, my Bey.

113
00:15:01,766 --> 00:15:04,376
They put the blame on each other.

114
00:15:07,175 --> 00:15:10,265
I want to say that
"let them wear away each other" but...

115
00:15:10,311 --> 00:15:13,071
What they do always end up
affecting us.

116
00:15:16,485 --> 00:15:19,075
Wind can only remove the dust
from a rock.

117
00:15:25,539 --> 00:15:30,599
So, the lords are scheming behind
each other...

118
00:15:36,577 --> 00:15:40,087
If we use their weakness,
the conquests are soon, brother.

119
00:15:41,459 --> 00:15:43,619
If our enemies are biting each other...

120
00:15:43,629 --> 00:15:45,819
then, we'll hunt them!

121
00:15:46,499 --> 00:15:50,939
İnegöl, Harmankaya, Bilecik...

122
00:15:52,505 --> 00:15:54,455
maybe Bursa.

123
00:15:58,529 --> 00:16:00,159
Why not?

124
00:16:09,506 --> 00:16:10,927
You are right, my bey but--

125
00:16:10,927 --> 00:16:14,587
Once we have all Turkmens
join our cause...

126
00:16:15,559 --> 00:16:20,729
once sisters bring joy to our tribe,
and we assure our unity...

127
00:16:22,845 --> 00:16:24,925
why not, Osman Bey?

128
00:16:27,197 --> 00:16:31,107
If it wasn't for the dream of
our ancestors, why would we be here?

129
00:16:34,288 --> 00:16:36,068
You are right.

130
00:16:37,747 --> 00:16:39,367
You are right.

131
00:16:42,134 --> 00:16:44,174
But firstly, Kosses...

132
00:16:45,618 --> 00:16:48,438
We'll watch him as a wolf watches
a sheep.

133
00:16:50,499 --> 00:16:52,609
We'll watch him and
find out...

134
00:16:53,482 --> 00:16:55,672
whom we will bite.

135
00:16:58,916 --> 00:17:03,606
Brother, we need to find a way to
put a spy next to Kosses.

136
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:08,540
May I enter, my bey?

137
00:17:09,166 --> 00:17:10,906
Come in.

138
00:17:18,519 --> 00:17:21,199
My bey, you summoned me.

139
00:17:22,817 --> 00:17:24,637
Release the Catalonian.

140
00:17:30,906 --> 00:17:33,886
Release him but follow him.

141
00:17:34,332 --> 00:17:36,232
Be his shadow.

142
00:17:36,807 --> 00:17:39,277
You'll know every step he makes,
Cerkutay.

143
00:17:43,189 --> 00:17:48,829
Once we find the moment, we'll
strike them like a lightning.

144
00:17:51,102 --> 00:17:52,922
As you order, my bey.

145
00:17:53,212 --> 00:17:56,532
We'll watch them like shadows
and hit them like lightning.

146
00:17:58,314 --> 00:18:01,764
Göktuğ, the alps should
sharpen their swords.

147
00:18:02,339 --> 00:18:05,719
They should get ready
for a campaign.

148
00:18:07,198 --> 00:18:08,718
As you order my bey.

149
00:18:22,036 --> 00:18:24,366
İnegöl Castle

150
00:18:28,059 --> 00:18:29,949
Hey! Get up!

151
00:18:33,011 --> 00:18:35,611
-Is he dead?
-I hope not.

152
00:18:35,753 --> 00:18:38,183
If he is, Lord Nikola kills
us all.

153
00:19:16,077 --> 00:19:20,517
My bey, Bala and I thought that we can't
prepare Mari's carpets in time.

154
00:19:21,712 --> 00:19:26,662
If you allow us, we want to gather
women from Kızılbey and other tribes.

155
00:19:27,281 --> 00:19:29,241
You thought well.

156
00:19:30,253 --> 00:19:34,063
We need to finish it before winter.
It will relieve the folk as well.

157
00:19:39,130 --> 00:19:41,180
My bey, may I enter?

158
00:19:42,084 --> 00:19:43,664
Come.

159
00:19:49,295 --> 00:19:52,085
My bey, Kutan is here.
He wishes to speak.

160
00:19:53,250 --> 00:19:54,550
Let him in.

161
00:20:03,768 --> 00:20:05,498
Osman Bey.

162
00:20:07,911 --> 00:20:09,151
Our tribe...

163
00:20:10,518 --> 00:20:12,318
Turgut Bey...

164
00:20:17,531 --> 00:20:20,181
Nikola raided our tribe.

165
00:20:28,387 --> 00:20:31,037
They showed no mercy
to the children and the women.

166
00:20:32,739 --> 00:20:34,419
He burnt the tribe.

167
00:20:34,849 --> 00:20:36,799
That vile man!

168
00:20:55,549 --> 00:20:57,009
Kutan.

169
00:20:59,137 --> 00:21:01,027
Raise your head.

170
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:05,043
What happened to Turgut Bey?

171
00:21:08,087 --> 00:21:09,997
He imprisoned Turgut Bey.

172
00:21:11,644 --> 00:21:14,124
We are without a head, Osman Bey.

173
00:21:15,486 --> 00:21:17,806
That vile heathen!

174
00:21:25,314 --> 00:21:30,044
Tell me, what does Turgut Bey have to
do with Nikola?

175
00:21:31,211 --> 00:21:33,121
I don't know, Osman Bey.

176
00:21:33,991 --> 00:21:35,461
I don't know.

177
00:21:36,380 --> 00:21:38,340
That vile dog!

178
00:21:40,507 --> 00:21:45,697
For all the Turks he made bleed,
I will rip his heart out.

179
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:58,070
Tell the people. I will save your bey
from that vile devil.

180
00:22:02,145 --> 00:22:03,785
-Boran.
-My bey.

181
00:22:04,085 --> 00:22:07,035
Go to Turgut Bey's tribe
with Kutan.

182
00:22:07,676 --> 00:22:10,026
Have enough alps with you.

183
00:22:10,848 --> 00:22:12,738
Do everything that needs to be done.

184
00:22:13,355 --> 00:22:15,175
As you order, my bey.

185
00:22:15,614 --> 00:22:17,764
May Allah bless you, Osman Bey.

186
00:22:19,562 --> 00:22:21,252
May Allah bless you.

187
00:22:33,562 --> 00:22:35,732
-Brother.
-My bey.

188
00:22:37,853 --> 00:22:40,743
Now, go to Nikola and ask for Turgut Bey.

189
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:45,882
He'll either give us Turgut Bey,
or his head.

190
00:22:46,583 --> 00:22:50,703
Either he'll give him, or I'll destroy
İnegöl to its last standing building.

191
00:22:54,121 --> 00:22:59,531
Tell him there will be retaliation for
all the Turks that he made bleed.

192
00:23:01,594 --> 00:23:03,244
Alright, my bey.

193
00:23:57,085 --> 00:23:59,325
Bravo, Turgut Bey.

194
00:23:59,586 --> 00:24:01,056
Bravo.

195
00:24:01,625 --> 00:24:03,545
You didn't disappoint me.

196
00:24:17,169 --> 00:24:19,349
What did I tell you, Argos.

197
00:24:20,275 --> 00:24:24,611
All these Turks are the same.
They have stubbornness.

198
00:24:24,611 --> 00:24:28,121
You can take their lives but not
their stubbornness.

199
00:24:32,508 --> 00:24:35,368
Slowly, shepherd.
Slowly.

200
00:24:37,804 --> 00:24:41,201
There is no need for wildness.
Don't worry,

201
00:24:41,201 --> 00:24:44,841
I'll hand you over to your new
owner soon.

202
00:24:47,207 --> 00:24:49,107
I won't kill you...

203
00:24:54,155 --> 00:24:58,785
with that, but with
these hands.

204
00:25:00,126 --> 00:25:04,426
My face will be the last face
you see in this world.

205
00:25:15,113 --> 00:25:17,453
Impossible, Turgut Bey.

206
00:25:18,944 --> 00:25:20,554
Impossible.

207
00:25:25,056 --> 00:25:28,246
Soldiers,
Take him away.

208
00:25:34,102 --> 00:25:35,532
Arbus.

209
00:25:37,872 --> 00:25:41,232
This gift is your responsibility.

210
00:25:42,026 --> 00:25:45,166
Have your eyes on him.

211
00:25:46,933 --> 00:25:50,323
- Mistakes... I don't...
- You don't like mistakes.

212
00:25:50,433 --> 00:25:52,153
I don't.

213
00:25:57,349 --> 00:25:59,839
Freaking shepherd.

214
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:20,620
You used to go yourself in such situations,
Osman Bey.

215
00:26:21,436 --> 00:26:23,846
Now you are sending a messenger.

216
00:26:27,953 --> 00:26:29,863
I am now Bey Osman.

217
00:26:35,761 --> 00:26:38,281
I am Osman who spreads
the seeds of a state.

218
00:26:42,216 --> 00:26:43,906
What makes me important...

219
00:26:46,290 --> 00:26:50,530
What makes a Bey important is his alps...

220
00:26:54,258 --> 00:26:56,058
His messengers...

221
00:26:57,521 --> 00:26:59,451
His sisters...

222
00:27:01,060 --> 00:27:03,140
...and his scholars.

223
00:27:05,932 --> 00:27:08,372
I want to build a system.

224
00:27:09,971 --> 00:27:12,311
A system that...

225
00:27:13,219 --> 00:27:16,169
everyone can find peace in it.

226
00:27:17,916 --> 00:27:25,056
Everyone including Muslims and non-Muslims
will want to be a part of it.

227
00:28:45,322 --> 00:28:47,182
It must be ready by tomorrow.

228
00:28:47,385 --> 00:28:49,605
It just needs a couple hand.
It'll be ready.

229
00:29:01,773 --> 00:29:03,973
Lord Aya Nicola is waiting for you.

230
00:29:19,168 --> 00:29:20,938
Gündüz Bey.

231
00:29:22,156 --> 00:29:24,006
You honored us.

232
00:29:26,572 --> 00:29:29,012
I like surprise guests.

233
00:29:29,033 --> 00:29:31,323
Lord Nicola, you know why I am here.

234
00:29:31,985 --> 00:29:33,805
It's Osman Bey's order.

235
00:29:34,557 --> 00:29:36,897
We want Turgut Bey,
whom you keep as a captive.

236
00:29:39,413 --> 00:29:44,153
What is your offer in return of such an
important thing, Gündüz Bey?

237
00:29:46,781 --> 00:29:48,241
Nothing.

238
00:29:55,585 --> 00:29:58,135
Osman Bey will take Turgut...

239
00:29:59,116 --> 00:30:04,436
...And he'll give me nothing
in return, yes?

240
00:30:08,774 --> 00:30:11,904
If you allow me.

241
00:30:17,636 --> 00:30:22,246
I like my meat bloody.
Rare.

242
00:30:22,246 --> 00:30:26,586
But every time, I get a wood-like
meat!

243
00:30:26,586 --> 00:30:29,186
Wood!

244
00:30:32,727 --> 00:30:37,737
As you see, Gündüz Bey.
You can't get everything you want.

245
00:30:37,737 --> 00:30:42,347
Lord Aya Nikola!
This is important!

246
00:30:43,472 --> 00:30:48,612
Turgut Bey is a Turkmen Bey. Osman Bey
would give his life but not him.

247
00:30:48,612 --> 00:30:52,612
It's in our laws.

248
00:30:54,717 --> 00:30:59,617
And be sure that we'll
obey that law.

249
00:30:59,888 --> 00:31:02,918
Your law.

250
00:31:02,918 --> 00:31:06,308
Your laws...

251
00:31:14,530 --> 00:31:18,050
Gündüz Bey.

252
00:31:19,398 --> 00:31:23,398
You consider yourself
to be the head of the Turkmens...

253
00:31:23,398 --> 00:31:27,398
but you can't
protect any of them.

254
00:31:28,603 --> 00:31:32,603
Turgut attacks my dear friend
Michael Kosses' sister...

255
00:31:32,603 --> 00:31:37,413
and kidnap her.
Will it go unpunished?

256
00:31:37,954 --> 00:31:41,364
Is that so?

257
00:31:41,364 --> 00:31:46,164
I will make him pay for what
he did to Mari.

258
00:31:46,510 --> 00:31:51,380
Nikola. I'm telling you
what Osman Bey says.

259
00:31:51,784 --> 00:31:55,784
It's up to you to listen to him or not.

260
00:31:55,784 --> 00:31:59,784
It's not up to me. If it was,
I still wouldn't give him.

261
00:31:59,784 --> 00:32:01,594
Yes, I wouldn't.

262
00:32:02,116 --> 00:32:07,536
I'll give him to Michael Kosses.
For Mari.

263
00:32:27,276 --> 00:32:30,926
My lions! Come on!

264
00:32:36,655 --> 00:32:41,445
Muslubeşe, your enemy raised
his sword.

265
00:32:41,445 --> 00:32:44,485
Where is your shield?

266
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:51,740
Don't let your enemy get closer
than the length of your spear.

267
00:32:51,740 --> 00:32:53,510
As you order, my bey.

268
00:32:55,754 --> 00:32:58,804
Alps!

269
00:33:03,195 --> 00:33:07,195
The enemy is out of control.

270
00:33:09,123 --> 00:33:14,443
Dishonorable Nikola raided
Turgut Bey's tribe...

271
00:33:14,719 --> 00:33:18,279
and imprisoned him.

272
00:33:18,981 --> 00:33:23,651
Just when our pain was fresh
about our martyrs, we added new ones.

273
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:27,710
When a Turkmen tribe burns...

274
00:33:27,710 --> 00:33:31,710
my heart burns.

275
00:33:32,259 --> 00:33:36,259
It's the day of unity!

276
00:33:36,259 --> 00:33:41,479
Gündüz Bey went to take Turgut Bey.

277
00:33:43,867 --> 00:33:47,867
If he returns empty handed...

278
00:33:48,189 --> 00:33:53,829
we'll crush down the walls
of Nikola upon him.

279
00:33:56,110 --> 00:34:00,110
A Turk can never be a slave!

280
00:34:01,790 --> 00:34:05,790
-Now equip your bloody weapons!
-As you order, my bey!

281
00:34:13,801 --> 00:34:17,471
Harmankaya Castle

282
00:34:17,471 --> 00:34:24,271
This Osman is still suspicious of me
about the alp issue.

283
00:34:25,768 --> 00:34:30,638
So, Mari, your brother needs to
make better moves.

284
00:34:31,069 --> 00:34:35,069
It's the thing you do the best, brother.

285
00:34:36,682 --> 00:34:42,002
Most importantly, I need to
take Father Gregor...

286
00:34:42,002 --> 00:34:46,002
from Osman's hands.

287
00:34:47,405 --> 00:34:51,285
I can't keep the Emperor
waiting.

288
00:34:51,285 --> 00:34:55,405
Osman is taking his steps carefully.
And he is determined.

289
00:34:55,405 --> 00:34:59,005
It won't be easy to take Gregor.

290
00:34:59,005 --> 00:35:02,765
Indeed.

291
00:35:02,765 --> 00:35:07,785
Sir, news from Aya Nikola.

292
00:35:07,785 --> 00:35:11,585
He said that he has Turgut.

293
00:35:13,092 --> 00:35:18,092
-He'll send him to you tomorrow.
-Good.

294
00:35:19,132 --> 00:35:23,132
Turgut is really important for Osman,
Mari.

295
00:35:24,282 --> 00:35:27,442
For some reason, he sees himself
responsible of everyone.

296
00:35:27,442 --> 00:35:31,992
Luck always sides with the powerful.

297
00:35:31,992 --> 00:35:36,282
Indeed.
Actually...

298
00:35:36,282 --> 00:35:39,322
he'll take Turgut and give Gregor.

299
00:35:46,647 --> 00:35:52,347
-Your wound can't wait any longer.
-Nothing is more important than this...

300
00:35:53,578 --> 00:35:56,238
including my life.

301
00:35:56,238 --> 00:36:02,608
But if it goes like this, they'll notice
my wound soon.

302
00:37:05,620 --> 00:37:09,620
He'll always be with us, Master Gregor.

303
00:37:15,508 --> 00:37:19,508
I live to protect you.

304
00:37:19,508 --> 00:37:23,508
I wish my death to be for the same cause.

305
00:37:26,299 --> 00:37:29,999
We need to protect it well.

306
00:37:29,999 --> 00:37:34,299
But how? We can't keep it on us.

307
00:37:34,299 --> 00:37:37,209
They might search us.

308
00:38:25,285 --> 00:38:29,285
We got a clue now.

309
00:38:29,285 --> 00:38:31,825
Baysungur.

310
00:38:36,320 --> 00:38:40,320
You stay here and watch them.

311
00:38:40,320 --> 00:38:44,320
I will go and tell my bey.

312
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:46,690
Come on.

313
00:38:59,479 --> 00:39:03,059
Bilecik Castle.

314
00:39:03,059 --> 00:39:07,809
Lately, we meet a lot, Lord Rogatus.

315
00:39:07,809 --> 00:39:12,979
Every time, your pursue gets
fatter.

316
00:39:12,979 --> 00:39:17,749
-You can't complain about that.
-I'm not complaining.

317
00:39:20,007 --> 00:39:25,097
Even though we couldn't get
Father Gregor, we were succesful.

318
00:39:25,630 --> 00:39:29,630
God is giving us another chance.

319
00:39:30,676 --> 00:39:36,056
Aya Nikola imprisoned a
Turkmen Bey named Turgut.

320
00:39:37,521 --> 00:39:41,851
This Turgut is very important
for Osman.

321
00:39:41,851 --> 00:39:46,851
-If we obtain him...
-It means that we have Father Gregor.

322
00:39:49,325 --> 00:39:53,995
According to what I heard from
my spies in Nikola's castle...

323
00:39:55,236 --> 00:40:00,316
Kosses will be going there personally
to take Turgut.

324
00:40:00,943 --> 00:40:05,633
Take Father Gregor for granted,
Lord Rogatus.

325
00:40:12,250 --> 00:40:16,250
Be careful.
He is a devil.

326
00:40:18,727 --> 00:40:24,367
Anselmo is always careful
against all devils.

327
00:40:26,720 --> 00:40:31,200
I'll bring Turgut to you,
don't doubt that.

328
00:40:54,644 --> 00:40:59,764
-Nikola will give Turgut to Kosses.
-Why is that, brother?

329
00:41:00,968 --> 00:41:07,118
He dotes upon Mari. He wants to
revenge her.

330
00:41:08,006 --> 00:41:13,096
That dog Nikola...
Why is he doing that?

331
00:41:13,999 --> 00:41:17,999
He wants to steal Mari's heart.

332
00:41:19,220 --> 00:41:23,220
Mari is single, my bey.
Nikola wants to marry her...

333
00:41:23,220 --> 00:41:27,660
and get her brother's support.
-Thank you.

334
00:41:31,452 --> 00:41:35,452
Then, we need to do an ambush
to save Turgut Bey.

335
00:41:35,452 --> 00:41:40,092
Nikola is getting prepared, Osman Bey.

336
00:41:41,656 --> 00:41:45,166
They are preparing a cage for Turgut.

337
00:41:45,870 --> 00:41:49,870
Soon, he'll give him to Kosses.

338
00:41:49,870 --> 00:41:53,490
This is the end of the words.

339
00:41:55,380 --> 00:42:00,620
Sharpen your swords.
For a single tear drop of a Turk...

340
00:42:00,620 --> 00:42:04,190
we can burn the whole world.

341
00:42:04,190 --> 00:42:08,920
My bey, what if it's all a trap?

342
00:42:10,044 --> 00:42:14,604
They know that you won't
leave him behind.

343
00:42:16,063 --> 00:42:20,063
What if they are trying
to lure you?

344
00:42:23,546 --> 00:42:27,546
But even if it's a trap...

345
00:42:27,546 --> 00:42:31,546
we need to find a way and
save Turgut Alp.

346
00:42:31,546 --> 00:42:35,546
We can't have the other tribes' support
when he is imprisoned.

347
00:42:35,546 --> 00:42:39,546
They should know that Osman Bey
won't leave anyone behind.

348
00:42:42,224 --> 00:42:45,554
Of course.

349
00:42:46,861 --> 00:42:50,861
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come in.

350
00:42:59,189 --> 00:43:02,009
We found it, my bey.

351
00:43:02,445 --> 00:43:07,065
We followed the wounded jackal and
it led us to it's den.

352
00:43:08,321 --> 00:43:12,981
But no one came or left.
Baysungur is still watching it, my bey.

353
00:43:13,861 --> 00:43:17,861
The wolf tasted blood.

354
00:43:18,450 --> 00:43:24,020
We are following them.
We'll bite them soon.

355
00:43:26,204 --> 00:43:30,204
But let's take care of this
Turgut issue first.

356
00:43:30,204 --> 00:43:33,064
Then, we'll march against
the Katalonians.

357
00:43:34,372 --> 00:43:38,372
We'll, my bey. We'll.

358
00:43:42,224 --> 00:43:46,904
Brother, get ready for the ambush.

359
00:43:48,487 --> 00:43:51,747
Alright, my bey.

360
00:44:47,217 --> 00:44:52,247
Gonca, you are responsible for
the carpets.

361
00:44:52,247 --> 00:44:55,137
Don't worry, Bala.

362
00:44:57,985 --> 00:45:03,025
Gökçe, help Gonca Hatun.

363
00:45:03,674 --> 00:45:07,474
Do as she says.

364
00:45:21,505 --> 00:45:26,725
Gökçe, it's not a thing that
you can do.

365
00:45:27,976 --> 00:45:32,516
Go and help the women out there.

366
00:45:33,157 --> 00:45:37,157
I can take care of the carpets.

367
00:46:50,630 --> 00:46:54,500
İnegöl Castle

368
00:46:57,483 --> 00:47:00,643
Welcome!

369
00:47:02,531 --> 00:47:05,731
Nikola!

370
00:47:06,473 --> 00:47:10,473
Why did you come all this way?

371
00:47:10,473 --> 00:47:13,443
I was going to send the gift
with soldiers.

372
00:47:13,722 --> 00:47:17,722
I'm happy to see you, dear Mari.

373
00:47:21,229 --> 00:47:26,719
The gift is so precious that I wanted
to come personally, Nikola.

374
00:47:26,990 --> 00:47:30,990
True. You should've seen him...

375
00:47:30,990 --> 00:47:35,860
when he was looking at his burned
tribe, Mari. This is nothing.

376
00:47:41,522 --> 00:47:45,522
Oh, your present is coming.

377
00:48:04,585 --> 00:48:08,585
Here is your present, dear Mari.

378
00:48:21,605 --> 00:48:26,665
Look, dear Mari.
Look at your gift.

379
00:48:31,035 --> 00:48:35,035
What did that wild wolf
turn into, right?

380
00:48:35,035 --> 00:48:38,485
He is like a pet now.

381
00:48:45,837 --> 00:48:49,837
Look how he sits...

382
00:48:49,837 --> 00:48:53,237
calm and quiet.

383
00:49:04,204 --> 00:49:07,304
Wild!

384
00:49:14,441 --> 00:49:20,681
We should understand him. His tribe
burnt down.

385
00:49:22,118 --> 00:49:25,418
His alps were murdered.

386
00:49:27,551 --> 00:49:32,291
So, he suffered a lot, dear Mari.
A lot.

387
00:49:36,856 --> 00:49:40,856
Right, Turgut Bey? Right?

388
00:50:11,328 --> 00:50:16,098
It's good that I came personally,
Nikola.

389
00:50:18,726 --> 00:50:23,716
-It's good.
-It's good, Kosses.

390
00:50:30,136 --> 00:50:33,216
It's good.

391
00:50:34,183 --> 00:50:38,183
Soldiers! Take him away.

392
00:50:48,583 --> 00:50:52,583
I'm thankful, Aya Nikola.

393
00:51:18,281 --> 00:51:22,281
Harmankaya's road divides
into two here.

394
00:51:23,401 --> 00:51:27,401
The river here overflows
this time of the year.

395
00:51:29,042 --> 00:51:33,932
I know it well. We rode a lot there.

396
00:51:35,736 --> 00:51:40,566
But, so does Kosses.

397
00:51:41,427 --> 00:51:45,227
So, he'll take this one.

398
00:51:46,815 --> 00:51:51,495
Göktuğ, Cerkutay.
You'll go in front.

399
00:51:52,129 --> 00:51:55,909
Saltuk, you'll attack from the
right flank.

400
00:51:55,909 --> 00:51:58,369
Alright, my bey.

401
00:52:18,709 --> 00:52:22,289
Keep your eyes open.

402
00:52:31,371 --> 00:52:35,371
Mari, you better keep your
eyes on the road.

403
00:52:35,371 --> 00:52:39,371
Do you think that Osman will
attack us, brother?

404
00:52:39,371 --> 00:52:42,381
What do you think?

405
00:53:31,439 --> 00:53:34,799
Anselmo...

406
00:53:45,445 --> 00:53:49,445
Your man gives my name to Osman...

407
00:53:49,445 --> 00:53:54,305
and you face me like an idiot. Did you
think there would be no consequences?

408
00:54:15,422 --> 00:54:18,912
Lord Kosses.

409
00:54:19,094 --> 00:54:23,094
This is all Rogatus' plans.

410
00:54:23,094 --> 00:54:27,344
Rogatus bought my man.

411
00:54:27,344 --> 00:54:31,344
You know, Catalonians like money.

412
00:54:36,890 --> 00:54:42,850
I was also betrayed. I have nothing
to do with this.

413
00:54:46,659 --> 00:54:50,659
Rogatus wants to use me
against you.

414
00:54:50,659 --> 00:54:54,659
He offered me a lot of money
for Turgut.

415
00:55:07,159 --> 00:55:12,109
-He'll set an ambush.
-Rogatus!

416
00:55:30,813 --> 00:55:37,473
I need to make good decisions to not
end up like this, Lord Kosses.

417
00:55:51,623 --> 00:55:55,623
How can I know that this is all...

418
00:55:55,623 --> 00:56:00,163
not a part of a plan that you
made with Rogatus?

419
00:56:01,841 --> 00:56:05,841
You know what you know, Lord Kosses.

420
00:56:06,945 --> 00:56:11,265
To believe, you shouldn't know.

421
00:56:27,445 --> 00:56:33,215
You don't have the numbers to fight with
Rogatus when he attacks you.

422
00:56:36,677 --> 00:56:41,397
If you take the chance to
lose Turgut...

423
00:56:41,397 --> 00:56:44,467
don't believe me.

424
00:56:53,716 --> 00:56:57,716
Like Osman wasn't enough...

425
00:57:07,926 --> 00:57:11,776
You will come to my ambush.

426
00:57:14,378 --> 00:57:19,458
-Osman?
-Osman, of course!

427
00:57:20,055 --> 00:57:24,055
Osman will surely make a move to
save Turgut.

428
00:57:25,414 --> 00:57:30,184
We mostly fight for gold, Lord Kosses.

429
00:57:31,551 --> 00:57:37,541
But there is something earned much
harder. It's trust.

430
00:57:57,331 --> 00:58:00,921
What do you want, pretty Byzantinian?

431
00:58:05,975 --> 00:58:09,865
Take your hand away!

432
00:58:29,947 --> 00:58:33,947
Why are you doing this?

433
00:58:34,697 --> 00:58:38,697
Why are you helping me?
Why?

434
00:58:51,006 --> 00:58:55,006
Anselmo wants to gain trust, Lord Kosses.

435
00:58:56,587 --> 00:59:01,257
You better use this chance well, Anselmo.

436
00:59:04,465 --> 00:59:07,555
For your own good.

437
00:59:13,207 --> 00:59:17,857
If we move the way you
were moving, we'll be on their lap.

438
00:59:20,400 --> 00:59:23,420
Let's go this way.

439
00:59:24,216 --> 00:59:28,216
No one uses this way because
of the risk of an overflow.

440
00:59:31,217 --> 00:59:34,837
You know Bhytinia well.

441
00:59:34,837 --> 00:59:39,217
You can't get away from Rogatus'
ambush in any other way.

442
00:59:41,120 --> 00:59:44,130
Alright.

443
00:59:45,041 --> 00:59:49,041
We'll listen to Anselmo's advice.

444
00:59:53,141 --> 00:59:55,251
Come on!

445
01:00:50,427 --> 01:00:53,407
Where are they.

446
01:00:53,407 --> 01:00:57,407
-They aren't coming.
-They will. Be patient.

447
01:00:58,274 --> 01:01:02,274
-They'll come.
-I can wait.

448
01:01:02,274 --> 01:01:05,554
But these ones can't wait for them.

449
01:01:10,021 --> 01:01:14,021
This silence isn't good.

450
01:01:15,179 --> 01:01:19,179
It isn't.

451
01:01:32,550 --> 01:01:35,690
No one is coming, my bey?

452
01:01:37,021 --> 01:01:42,281
They'll come. Wait.
They'll come.

453
01:01:43,302 --> 01:01:46,442
Alright, my bey.

454
01:01:59,423 --> 01:02:03,423
My bey, the catalonians...

455
01:02:03,423 --> 01:02:08,903
I was following them.
They united with Kosses' troops.

456
01:02:10,643 --> 01:02:15,603
-Then?
-It was like they weren't expected.

457
01:02:16,000 --> 01:02:21,240
Kosses' soldiers drew their swords,
then things calmed down. They united.

458
01:02:22,506 --> 01:02:26,506
My bey,Anselmo and Kosses talked
for a while.

459
01:02:26,506 --> 01:02:28,916
Then, they changed the road.

460
01:02:38,929 --> 01:02:40,939
Alps!

461
01:02:49,913 --> 01:02:52,153
My bey.

462
01:02:52,276 --> 01:02:57,026
Get ready at once!
We'll stop them. Come on!

463
01:03:33,095 --> 01:03:35,635
Lord Kosses.

464
01:03:36,243 --> 01:03:40,593
Who is this Turgut?

465
01:03:40,593 --> 01:03:46,343
Why does Osman want him? He must
be important.

466
01:03:46,851 --> 01:03:51,411
He is not important. Just an ordinary
Turkish bey.

467
01:03:52,457 --> 01:03:56,457
Osman and Turkic laws.

468
01:03:56,457 --> 01:03:59,787
Who knows what non-sense
reasons he has.

469
01:03:59,975 --> 01:04:02,245
What about you?

470
01:04:03,914 --> 01:04:07,914
He is my enemy, Anselmo.

471
01:04:07,914 --> 01:04:11,194
I think this explanation
is enough for you.

472
01:04:53,877 --> 01:04:59,557
-What's this, Anselmo? Why did we stop?
-Lord Kosses.

473
01:05:35,326 --> 01:05:37,946
I am taking Turgut, Lord Kosses.

474
01:05:52,888 --> 01:05:56,178
You sold me out to Rogatus, didn't you?

475
01:05:58,076 --> 01:06:00,766
Your loyalty is only to gold, right?

476
01:06:02,764 --> 01:06:04,924
Let Turgut go, Kosses.

477
01:06:05,026 --> 01:06:12,686
Let him go so that I spare your and your
beautiful sister's life.

478
01:06:13,167 --> 01:06:15,567
I will never surrender.

479
01:06:16,600 --> 01:06:18,590
I won't give you what you want!

480
01:06:19,296 --> 01:06:22,626
And God is my witness I will kill you
myself!

481
01:06:29,130 --> 01:06:31,170
Don't be stupid, Kosses!

482
01:06:31,350 --> 01:06:33,380
All I want is Turgut!

483
01:06:40,775 --> 01:06:44,775
Also, you were the one telling he was
worthless.

484
01:07:12,614 --> 01:07:14,354
All right!

485
01:07:17,079 --> 01:07:18,849
Turgut is yours.

486
01:07:19,870 --> 01:07:22,270
Soldiers, let them take him.

487
01:07:54,393 --> 01:07:56,523
Osman!

488
01:08:02,868 --> 01:08:04,698
Osman Bey!

489
01:08:05,145 --> 01:08:08,775
Take him down!
Take him down!

490
01:08:11,306 --> 01:08:12,676
Come on, alps!

491
01:08:20,434 --> 01:08:21,824
Mari!

492
01:08:21,824 --> 01:08:23,074
Brother!

493
01:08:24,417 --> 01:08:25,987
Mari, stay with me!

494
01:08:31,976 --> 01:08:33,286
Stay behind me!

495
01:09:14,641 --> 01:09:17,431
Damn it! Don't miss him!
Catch him!

496
01:09:17,809 --> 01:09:19,329
Damn it!

497
01:09:23,287 --> 01:09:27,737
Alps! Don't let them breathe!
Come on!

498
01:09:38,998 --> 01:09:40,368
Brother!

499
01:09:40,673 --> 01:09:42,073
Attack!

500
01:10:32,067 --> 01:10:35,117
Attack!
Attack!

501
01:11:40,870 --> 01:11:43,440
They only strengthen our anger by running.

502
01:11:44,411 --> 01:11:46,041
What do we do now, my Bey?

503
01:11:47,561 --> 01:11:51,561
We know where Turgut Bey is going.

504
01:11:52,910 --> 01:11:54,000
Come on!

505
01:12:16,665 --> 01:12:18,145
Oh no!

506
01:12:22,167 --> 01:12:23,967
What am I going to tell Bala?

507
01:12:38,246 --> 01:12:39,986
Hello, hatuns.

508
01:12:43,910 --> 01:12:45,300
Gonca?

509
01:12:47,919 --> 01:12:49,439
What happened here?

510
01:12:50,659 --> 01:12:52,379
What happened to these?

511
01:12:57,531 --> 01:13:00,281
What is this, hatuns?
Who would do this?

512
01:13:01,416 --> 01:13:03,036
Tell me how this happened!

513
01:13:07,331 --> 01:13:09,021
We don't know, Bala.

514
01:13:09,644 --> 01:13:10,884
No one saw anything.

515
01:13:10,884 --> 01:13:12,474
I ask you Gonca!

516
01:13:12,529 --> 01:13:14,369
Didn't we trust you with them?

517
01:13:18,134 --> 01:13:22,134
Didn't we tell you to look after the rugs?

518
01:13:22,829 --> 01:13:24,829
Is this how you fulfill your duty?

519
01:13:24,951 --> 01:13:28,951
My Bala, it happened overnight.
I--

520
01:13:28,951 --> 01:13:30,101
I gave you a duty!

521
01:13:35,672 --> 01:13:37,392
I didn't tell you to make excuses!

522
01:13:39,260 --> 01:13:41,550
There is nothing to do anymore,
Bala Hatun.

523
01:13:44,588 --> 01:13:45,938
Mistakes happen.

524
01:13:45,938 --> 01:13:47,808
Is this a mistake to make, Mahur Hatun?

525
01:13:47,906 --> 01:13:49,766
How will we make up for that many rugs?

526
01:13:49,866 --> 01:13:51,756
We were barely making them.

527
01:13:55,259 --> 01:13:57,779
Hatuns, separate the good ones.

528
01:13:57,779 --> 01:13:59,379
Let's see how many are missing.

529
01:14:00,184 --> 01:14:03,824
Let's see so that we can make up for them,
Bala Hatun.

530
01:15:59,243 --> 01:16:03,833
My Bey, when we followed them
they came here.

531
01:16:06,840 --> 01:16:08,780
They moved, obviously.

532
01:16:51,158 --> 01:16:54,088
Osman wouldn't let us go while we had...

533
01:16:55,256 --> 01:16:57,526
...such a treasure as Turgut.

534
01:17:08,018 --> 01:17:09,738
He is capable of doing anything.

535
01:17:11,505 --> 01:17:15,085
You are right, Commander Anselmo.

536
01:17:16,435 --> 01:17:18,945
He can never find us here.

537
01:17:53,738 --> 01:17:55,518
This wound is pierced.

538
01:17:58,633 --> 01:18:00,253
Tell me, how did this wound
happen?

539
01:18:01,878 --> 01:18:03,368
It happened while running away.

540
01:18:06,661 --> 01:18:08,201
When Master Gregor fell.

541
01:18:09,334 --> 01:18:13,504
I've seen many runaways, many injured but
their wounds were not like this.

542
01:18:54,061 --> 01:18:55,761
In the name of Allah, the merciful.

543
01:19:10,266 --> 01:19:12,676
If this Anselmo was Kosses' man...

544
01:19:16,205 --> 01:19:18,255
...then he wouldn't...

545
01:19:20,616 --> 01:19:22,776
...draw his sword to him.

546
01:19:25,622 --> 01:19:30,522
They would draw their sword to both Kosses
and Rogatus.

547
01:19:31,842 --> 01:19:33,632
They are hard to understand.

548
01:19:36,615 --> 01:19:38,985
Then, this Anselmo must have...

549
01:19:39,769 --> 01:19:42,099
...set a trap to Kosses too.

550
01:19:42,920 --> 01:19:44,380
It wasn't for Kosses.

551
01:19:45,288 --> 01:19:48,118
He also tried to take Gregor from Rogatus.

552
01:19:48,768 --> 01:19:50,648
Their only value is gold, brother.

553
01:19:52,239 --> 01:19:55,819
They are dogs for whoever gives
their coin.

554
01:19:58,535 --> 01:20:02,535
But soon, I will expose all their games
one by one.

555
01:20:05,702 --> 01:20:06,972
I hope.

556
01:20:07,864 --> 01:20:09,414
Can we enter, my Bey?

557
01:20:11,271 --> 01:20:12,631
Come in, Saltuk.

558
01:20:20,274 --> 01:20:23,124
My Bey, Father Gregor is wounded.

559
01:20:23,715 --> 01:20:25,215
He doesn't look good.

560
01:20:58,877 --> 01:21:00,997
How is Father Gregor?

561
01:21:02,299 --> 01:21:04,419
There is a wound on his arm, my Bey.

562
01:21:05,164 --> 01:21:06,884
It's like a deep hollow.

563
01:21:10,131 --> 01:21:11,611
How is it now?

564
01:21:12,963 --> 01:21:16,093
I put ointment on it. His wound will heal
but...

565
01:21:17,061 --> 01:21:20,491
...I've seen many accidents, many wounded
people but never a wound like this.

566
01:21:20,574 --> 01:21:24,224
It neither looks like a dagger wound nor
a sword wound.

567
01:21:27,602 --> 01:21:29,382
So, it's not a cut you say?

568
01:21:32,839 --> 01:21:34,779
Could it be an animal attack?

569
01:21:35,680 --> 01:21:37,390
There were no teeth marks either.

570
01:21:38,718 --> 01:21:40,488
It looks carved.

571
01:21:48,142 --> 01:21:49,912
Carved, huh?

572
01:22:17,319 --> 01:22:19,539
Are you feeling better, Father Gregor?

573
01:22:20,836 --> 01:22:22,306
Get well soon.

574
01:22:22,877 --> 01:22:26,267
I am better. Thank you, Osman Bey.

575
01:22:30,639 --> 01:22:32,739
Kumral Abdal is a skilled healer.

576
01:22:33,262 --> 01:22:36,832
He sure will heal you.
Don't worry.

577
01:22:42,254 --> 01:22:44,594
Your life is under our protection.

578
01:22:50,386 --> 01:22:52,996
Please continue to rest.

579
01:23:12,945 --> 01:23:17,505
Hatuns, you didn't turn me down and come.
Thank you.

580
01:23:17,579 --> 01:23:19,969
Thank you, Mahur Hatun.

581
01:23:19,969 --> 01:23:21,989
We had a few problems at first.

582
01:23:22,665 --> 01:23:24,695
But we managed, thankfully.

583
01:23:26,487 --> 01:23:31,947
What I want from you is to show the skills
of Kızılbey Hatuns to everyone.

584
01:23:32,875 --> 01:23:38,545
If people like these rugs, it will be good
for our trade and our tribe.

585
01:23:40,247 --> 01:23:44,247
I have absolute trust in you.
Don't disappoint me.

586
01:23:45,602 --> 01:23:47,762
Come on, good luck.

587
01:23:47,813 --> 01:23:50,343
Thank you, Mahur Hatun.

588
01:24:27,433 --> 01:24:29,333
Whose dog are you?

589
01:24:32,344 --> 01:24:34,234
Why are you standing there?

590
01:24:37,240 --> 01:24:40,240
Speak, heretic!
Speak.

591
01:25:01,563 --> 01:25:04,123
I won't forget this face.

592
01:25:06,809 --> 01:25:09,069
You will pay for this, for sure.

593
01:25:10,193 --> 01:25:11,663
I won't forget.

594
01:25:15,533 --> 01:25:19,093
Everyone is after you, Turgut.

595
01:25:21,030 --> 01:25:22,850
People love you.

596
01:25:24,391 --> 01:25:25,751
However...

597
01:25:27,613 --> 01:25:30,013
... the one that has more money will
get you...

598
01:25:32,431 --> 01:25:36,431
... not the one that loves you more.

599
01:25:45,036 --> 01:25:46,946
Turgut!

600
01:25:48,454 --> 01:25:51,714
I wonder how many of these you are worth.

601
01:25:55,152 --> 01:25:57,122
Do you think they were cheap, Turgut?

602
01:26:00,222 --> 01:26:03,562
No, no.

603
01:26:04,173 --> 01:26:10,753
If my name is Turgut Bey, I will make you
swallow those coins with their bag.

604
01:26:13,374 --> 01:26:16,704
I will send you to hell with them.

605
01:26:18,201 --> 01:26:20,591
Lord Rogatus is coming.

606
01:27:01,878 --> 01:27:07,488
Looks like you had a hard time trying to
find us, Lord Rogatus.

607
01:27:08,804 --> 01:27:11,454
You are a simple man, Anselmo.

608
01:27:13,877 --> 01:27:19,797
Both guessing you would move and sending
someone after you was easy.

609
01:27:21,759 --> 01:27:25,009
Look at this, look!
What is this?

610
01:27:25,024 --> 01:27:26,254
Dirt.

611
01:27:27,646 --> 01:27:31,146
My priceless cape is covered in dirt.

612
01:27:33,961 --> 01:27:36,411
Why though?
I knew this would happen.

613
01:27:36,411 --> 01:27:40,021
But why do I come here anyway?
What do you think?

614
01:27:40,608 --> 01:27:45,478
Anselmo is sorry about this. My men will
clean it at once.

615
01:27:52,750 --> 01:27:59,080
So, Turgut is valuable enough to cover
your nice clothes in the dirt.

616
01:28:06,359 --> 01:28:10,359
Right now, I should have been in
my castle.

617
01:28:10,687 --> 01:28:13,837
Turgut should've been with me and
my clothes should've been clean.

618
01:28:20,025 --> 01:28:24,785
Why is Turgut here?
Why did you bring him here?

619
01:28:25,723 --> 01:28:34,163
Because I think I accepted less than
his worth, Lord Rogatus.

620
01:28:36,756 --> 01:28:39,486
Therefore, I am keeping Turgut.

621
01:28:43,170 --> 01:28:44,490
I get it.

622
01:29:39,837 --> 01:29:41,177
Diego.

623
01:29:43,211 --> 01:29:44,741
Bring Turgut.

624
01:30:14,529 --> 01:30:16,139
He is a noble man...

625
01:30:16,988 --> 01:30:21,378
...is always loyal to his promise.

626
01:30:27,727 --> 01:30:30,097
You owe that purse of gold to this.

627
01:30:35,931 --> 01:30:39,581
Get yourself some clothes with them.

628
01:30:40,027 --> 01:30:41,797
You dress terribly.

629
01:31:12,909 --> 01:31:16,449
I want this great news to Osman Bey
in person.

630
01:31:45,334 --> 01:31:46,824
Can we enter, my Bey?

631
01:31:49,116 --> 01:31:50,356
Come in.

632
01:31:56,723 --> 01:32:01,023
My Bey, Rogatus the Lord of Bilecik is
here to see you.

633
01:32:20,988 --> 01:32:22,628
I will keep it short, Osman Bey.

634
01:32:25,340 --> 01:32:30,860
You told me you didn't know where
Father Gregor was although he was here.

635
01:32:30,860 --> 01:32:33,730
Now, we both know the truth.

636
01:32:35,303 --> 01:32:38,013
You said you would keep it short.

637
01:32:39,812 --> 01:32:41,792
Tell me.

638
01:32:43,237 --> 01:32:45,057
Our terms are equal now.

639
01:32:47,504 --> 01:32:51,504
I didn't come here empty-handed to
take my friend Gregor.

640
01:32:52,411 --> 01:32:54,861
I have something that is valuable for you.

641
01:32:58,694 --> 01:33:00,194
Turgut.

642
01:33:05,538 --> 01:33:10,408
If Turgut is important to you as much as
I heard...

643
01:33:11,023 --> 01:33:15,023
...you will bring Father Gregor to Çakırcı
at noon, tomorrow.

644
01:33:19,164 --> 01:33:21,854
He is not important to me.
He will die if you don't come.

645
01:33:50,525 --> 01:33:54,065
So, it was Rogatus all along.

646
01:33:55,600 --> 01:33:58,100
They took Turgut to give to him.

647
01:34:03,777 --> 01:34:05,717
Gather the beys.

648
01:34:06,291 --> 01:34:08,711
We will discuss this.

649
01:34:09,852 --> 01:34:11,562
As you command, my Bey.

650
01:34:15,490 --> 01:34:19,490
Harmankaya Castle

651
01:34:19,941 --> 01:34:21,891
Tell me, Bahadır.

652
01:34:22,899 --> 01:34:26,339
What news did you bring to us from
the Kayı Tribe?

653
01:34:27,688 --> 01:34:31,688
Does Osman have Turgut or not?

654
01:34:34,073 --> 01:34:35,773
No, he doesn't.

655
01:34:43,558 --> 01:34:45,718
Osman Bey couldn't get Turgut.

656
01:34:48,903 --> 01:34:50,723
Don't worry.

657
01:34:51,469 --> 01:34:53,689
He will get him eventually.

658
01:34:54,537 --> 01:34:56,797
What does that meanü Lord Kosses?

659
01:34:57,904 --> 01:35:00,624
Since Turgut isn't with Osman...

660
01:35:03,583 --> 01:35:06,383
...he is with Anselmo...

661
01:35:08,651 --> 01:35:10,621
... who sold me out to Rogatus.

662
01:35:16,630 --> 01:35:18,240
Then Roga--

663
01:35:25,885 --> 01:35:31,625
In this case, Rogatus will give Turgut and
take Gregor.

664
01:35:35,177 --> 01:35:37,687
If this happens...

665
01:35:39,147 --> 01:35:44,877
...my reputation in King's head will be
terribly hurt, Mari.

666
01:35:46,350 --> 01:35:48,440
Terribly.

667
01:36:21,670 --> 01:36:29,390
If you give Father Gregor and take Turgut,
your people will say that...

668
01:36:29,528 --> 01:36:32,748
... you are showing weakness.

669
01:36:36,164 --> 01:36:43,144
If you don't, a Turkmen Bey will be
held captive by the infidel...

670
01:36:44,448 --> 01:36:48,448
...and you will violate the tradition.

671
01:36:50,876 --> 01:36:52,836
You are right, my Sheik.

672
01:36:53,605 --> 01:36:57,605
Either way is not suitable.

673
01:36:59,287 --> 01:37:01,557
This is a bad situation.

674
01:37:05,497 --> 01:37:10,277
While Sultan Izzettin was a prisoner in
the Byzantine dungeons didn't Berke Han...

675
01:37:10,344 --> 01:37:17,944
... send an army for him from across
the seas, from the Crimea to Byzantium?

676
01:37:19,823 --> 01:37:26,193
Sure. To him, my master Sarı Saltuk
told...

677
01:37:27,919 --> 01:37:29,939
... to follow the tradition.

678
01:37:30,474 --> 01:37:33,504
The Turkish Sultan will not be a prisoner,
he said.

679
01:37:36,910 --> 01:37:38,570
This is a bad situation.

680
01:37:40,068 --> 01:37:44,068
To show weakness in the eyes of the enemy
or...

681
01:37:46,115 --> 01:37:51,105
... to leave a Turkmen Bey to the enemy's
hands.

682
01:37:56,121 --> 01:37:57,591
It is a tough choice.

683
01:37:59,459 --> 01:38:01,649
There is no easy for us, my Sheik.

684
01:38:02,210 --> 01:38:04,350
There is no easy for us.

685
01:38:05,410 --> 01:38:10,970
We testify that you are with Allah,
Osman Bey.

686
01:38:13,457 --> 01:38:16,747
Those who are with Allah always
struggle.

687
01:38:19,679 --> 01:38:22,319
What does it say in the book?

688
01:38:22,864 --> 01:38:24,954
In the Surah Inshirah.

689
01:38:26,341 --> 01:38:29,091
In the name of Allah, the merciful.

690
01:38:29,642 --> 01:38:31,802
Almighty Allah says...

691
01:38:32,197 --> 01:38:35,777
...''In the name of Allah, the merciful.''

692
01:38:37,565 --> 01:38:40,935
''Didn't we open up your heart?''

693
01:38:43,380 --> 01:38:48,160
''Didn't we remove the weight that
bent your back?''

694
01:38:49,808 --> 01:38:53,438
''Have we not exalted your glory?''

695
01:38:54,950 --> 01:39:00,780
So with hardship, there is ease.

696
01:39:01,368 --> 01:39:02,498
Yes.

697
01:39:03,239 --> 01:39:09,139
Every hardship comes with ease.

698
01:39:12,730 --> 01:39:19,930
So when you have finished,
get up and turn only to your Rabb.

699
01:39:21,774 --> 01:39:23,374
Amen, my Sheik.
Amen.

700
01:39:23,748 --> 01:39:25,178
I hope...

701
01:39:28,182 --> 01:39:33,472
... I will follow the tradition and
take Turgut back...

702
01:39:33,812 --> 01:39:38,802
... and I will not leave Father Gregor
to them.

703
01:39:40,559 --> 01:39:43,719
I hope, Osman Bey.
I hope.

704
01:39:45,546 --> 01:39:49,546
Let alone asking how,
I am not even curious.

705
01:39:50,388 --> 01:39:55,518
We know that some works of the Beys are
secret.

706
01:39:55,815 --> 01:39:58,855
No way, my Sheik.

707
01:39:59,590 --> 01:40:04,730
As always, you enlightened us with
your beautiful words.

708
01:40:06,724 --> 01:40:10,724
You gave us a calm breath.

709
01:40:11,356 --> 01:40:13,036
May Allah be pleased with you.

710
01:40:13,216 --> 01:40:16,126
Peace of mind, my Bey.
Peace of mind.

711
01:40:17,578 --> 01:40:21,578
It exactly means what you have said
in Turkish.

712
01:40:37,143 --> 01:40:38,363
Good job.

713
01:40:48,658 --> 01:40:50,698
You have a guest, Bala.

714
01:41:22,836 --> 01:41:24,176
Welcome, Mari.

715
01:41:24,176 --> 01:41:25,306
Thank you, Bala Hatun.

716
01:41:26,086 --> 01:41:27,956
You came to see the rugs, I believe.

717
01:41:27,987 --> 01:41:30,717
-The rugs are here, Here you go.
-Before that...

718
01:41:32,465 --> 01:41:34,955
...I'd like to talk to you about something
important.

719
01:41:37,499 --> 01:41:39,119
Yes, Mari?

720
01:42:10,307 --> 01:42:11,967
What is this, Mari?

721
01:42:14,875 --> 01:42:17,425
The dagger that I gave to
Turgut's scabbard.

722
01:42:18,782 --> 01:42:20,582
Turgut Bey?

723
01:42:21,822 --> 01:42:23,362
Yesterday...

724
01:42:24,041 --> 01:42:26,181
...I helped Turgut running away.

725
01:42:27,012 --> 01:42:31,012
This scabbard is of the dagger I gave him.

726
01:42:32,100 --> 01:42:33,860
He got away thanks to me.

727
01:42:35,249 --> 01:42:36,469
Why?

728
01:42:37,426 --> 01:42:40,666
I wanted to give Turgut to you
but I couldn't.

729
01:42:41,626 --> 01:42:43,466
I wanted you to know that.

730
01:42:44,871 --> 01:42:46,231
By the way...

731
01:42:46,559 --> 01:42:49,959
...I'd be glad if you conveyed what I told
to Osman Bey too.

732
01:42:52,718 --> 01:42:54,358
Thank you, Mari.

733
01:42:57,165 --> 01:43:00,735
Don't worry.
I will tell Osman Bey.

734
01:43:02,034 --> 01:43:04,604
Come on, let's take a look at the rugs.

735
01:43:35,591 --> 01:43:37,651
You seem well, Father Gregor.

736
01:43:39,284 --> 01:43:41,194
Do you have any pain?

737
01:43:41,515 --> 01:43:44,905
Thank you, Osman Bey. I don't have much
pain left.

738
01:43:45,552 --> 01:43:47,692
I believe my wound is healing quickly.

739
01:43:50,539 --> 01:43:55,479
If you are feeling well,
then you can get ready.

740
01:44:01,718 --> 01:44:03,818
You are going to Rogatus.

741
01:44:28,440 --> 01:44:29,940
What?

742
01:44:31,134 --> 01:44:33,254
How did this happen, Andreas?

743
01:44:33,868 --> 01:44:37,868
Did I miss something while
I was unconscious?

744
01:44:39,714 --> 01:44:41,884
Everything was the same, Master Gregor.

745
01:44:44,709 --> 01:44:47,299
This is Lord Rogatus' doing, obviously.

746
01:44:47,818 --> 01:44:49,268
Obviously.

747
01:44:51,119 --> 01:44:55,189
What matters is that we are getting out of
this hell, Master.

748
01:45:20,014 --> 01:45:21,384
Beautiful.

749
01:45:21,803 --> 01:45:22,993
It's like a painting.

750
01:45:24,051 --> 01:45:25,961
Our Hatuns did it.

751
01:45:26,344 --> 01:45:28,584
It's doesn't bleed colors, it
doesn't blench.

752
01:45:29,173 --> 01:45:32,173
They did it with their own hands.

753
01:45:32,519 --> 01:45:37,509
Bala Hatun, I want your rugs in
Harmankaya Palace.

754
01:45:39,882 --> 01:45:42,262
With pleasure.

755
01:45:49,055 --> 01:45:51,485
We should think of every possibility.

756
01:45:51,670 --> 01:45:54,410
I don't want any trouble.

757
01:45:56,639 --> 01:45:59,049
We have warned the soldiers, sir.

758
01:46:08,300 --> 01:46:09,390
Osman...

759
01:46:11,181 --> 01:46:14,551
will try to trick us even he gives
us Gregor back.

760
01:46:15,835 --> 01:46:18,225
Be careful.

761
01:46:24,362 --> 01:46:28,642
After we take Gregor, when we go
back to the castle...

762
01:46:29,464 --> 01:46:31,844
we will use the oldest route.

763
01:46:33,786 --> 01:46:37,786
It will protect us from possible traps.

764
01:46:40,197 --> 01:46:45,497
The place we will meet in matters too.
Choose your best men, place them around.

765
01:46:45,788 --> 01:46:49,258
- Just in case.
- Your command.

766
01:46:59,145 --> 01:47:01,995
He won't take Gregor...

767
01:47:02,654 --> 01:47:04,984
whatever he does.

768
01:48:44,042 --> 01:48:46,602
I'm grateful that you kept your word.

769
01:48:51,101 --> 01:48:55,981
I hope that our friendship
will be honored one day.

770
01:48:57,982 --> 01:49:00,422
Allah knows, Rogatus.

771
01:49:02,076 --> 01:49:04,046
Maybe, one day.

772
01:49:37,044 --> 01:49:38,874
Come on.

773
01:50:54,107 --> 01:50:56,557
Are you okay, Turgut Bey?

774
01:50:57,624 --> 01:50:59,954
Are you hurt?

775
01:51:01,535 --> 01:51:02,425
Come on.

776
01:51:04,422 --> 01:51:07,462
Let's go to the tent, Kumral Abdal will
take care of you.

777
01:51:10,656 --> 01:51:12,846
Bring Turgut Bey's horse.

778
01:51:17,044 --> 01:51:19,404
Thank you, Osman Bey.

779
01:51:21,167 --> 01:51:23,827
I owe you a life.

780
01:51:26,983 --> 01:51:29,093
Thank you.

781
01:51:42,659 --> 01:51:44,569
However...

782
01:51:49,571 --> 01:51:53,571
don't interfere with my business anymore.

783
01:51:56,554 --> 01:51:59,884
I don't want any help from you.

784
01:52:03,924 --> 01:52:07,214
My tent is mine, your
tent is yours.

785
01:52:07,418 --> 01:52:10,988
Your enemy bothers you, my enemy
bothers me.

786
01:52:11,680 --> 01:52:16,960
Don't go into my way anymore, Osman Bey.

787
01:52:21,235 --> 01:52:23,105
How dare you!

788
01:52:43,234 --> 01:52:45,894
We have to cut his tongue.

789
01:52:47,708 --> 01:52:50,708
All the suffering...

790
01:52:50,957 --> 01:52:53,777
Our Bey tried so hard to get the Priest.

791
01:52:55,008 --> 01:52:57,998
Now, for a rebellious Bey...

792
01:53:02,511 --> 01:53:04,881
You will settle down, Turgut Bey.

793
01:53:09,348 --> 01:53:12,168
You only burn where you touch now.

794
01:53:13,832 --> 01:53:16,522
When your fire stops...

795
01:53:18,640 --> 01:53:20,780
When you stop...

796
01:53:23,191 --> 01:53:25,841
then we will be together.

797
01:54:04,649 --> 01:54:08,649
Rogatus, may God bless you.

798
01:54:08,999 --> 01:54:11,669
May God's love always be with you.

799
01:54:11,958 --> 01:54:14,288
Thanks to you, I'm here.

800
01:54:15,020 --> 01:54:19,110
Don't think about these things.
You're already tired.

801
01:54:19,396 --> 01:54:24,936
Have a rest, please. We have lots
of time to talk.

802
01:54:28,969 --> 01:54:30,359
Your arm..

803
01:54:34,373 --> 01:54:38,443
- Did Osman do something bad?
- It's not important.

804
01:54:38,691 --> 01:54:41,221
It's just an accident.

805
01:55:40,164 --> 01:55:44,264
- Welcome, our Bey!
- Thank you.

806
01:55:47,167 --> 01:55:48,617
Thank you.

807
01:55:49,575 --> 01:55:51,815
Welcome, my Bey.

808
01:55:59,761 --> 01:56:03,541
Are you okay, my Bey? How did Nikola
let you go?

809
01:56:04,121 --> 01:56:07,271
Forget about me. How's my tent?

810
01:56:07,915 --> 01:56:10,355
We're fine.

811
01:56:11,032 --> 01:56:15,902
You did a good job.

812
01:56:16,006 --> 01:56:20,266
- Thank you, Kutay.
- Thanks to Osman Bey...

813
01:56:20,577 --> 01:56:24,647
he didn't leave us alone.
How did you come here?

814
01:56:25,465 --> 01:56:28,635
It's complicated.

815
01:56:28,920 --> 01:56:31,790
Osman Bey tried hard.

816
01:56:32,551 --> 01:56:37,981
Thanks to him. He's a brave man.

817
01:56:38,044 --> 01:56:39,474
Don't forget, Kutay.

818
01:56:39,980 --> 01:56:45,130
If Osman Bey didn't withdraw us, none of
it would happen.

819
01:56:47,388 --> 01:56:49,838
It's time for revenge.

820
01:56:49,944 --> 01:56:51,314
Nikola...

821
01:56:51,896 --> 01:56:52,786
Kosses...

822
01:56:53,225 --> 01:56:56,175
We will kill them all.

823
01:56:56,520 --> 01:56:59,480
- My Bey.
- We will.

824
01:56:59,965 --> 01:57:04,975
We will take revenge for what happened,
We won't sleep until we will.

825
01:57:05,801 --> 01:57:07,761
Don't forget that.

826
01:57:22,812 --> 01:57:28,452
(She sings a lullaby)
"May the tent be with you."

827
01:57:29,015 --> 01:57:34,425
"May your food be sweet."

828
01:57:34,819 --> 01:57:39,979
Sleep, my son, sleep.

829
01:57:40,884 --> 01:57:45,194
Sleep, my son, sleep.

830
01:57:50,674 --> 01:57:53,914
I see, you don't
want to sleep.

831
01:57:56,997 --> 01:58:01,697
Gökçe, who do you
think did it?

832
01:58:05,092 --> 01:58:07,612
I don't know, Malhun Hatun.

833
01:58:18,224 --> 01:58:20,624
Put Osman to the bed.

834
01:58:31,416 --> 01:58:33,346
Your face...

835
01:58:34,658 --> 01:58:38,058
was different when Bala Hatun
said something.

836
01:58:41,149 --> 01:58:43,929
I don't understand, Malhun Hatun.

837
01:59:02,196 --> 01:59:04,576
What are you doing, Malhun Hatun?

838
01:59:08,033 --> 01:59:10,963
What's it that, Gökçe?

839
01:59:11,917 --> 01:59:14,027
What's that!

840
01:59:16,229 --> 01:59:19,009
You did it, right?

841
01:59:28,696 --> 01:59:31,366
Malhun Hatun, I---

842
01:59:44,197 --> 01:59:47,607
Swear you won't do something
like that again!

843
01:59:50,755 --> 01:59:54,755
Go away! I don't
want to see you.

844
02:00:46,622 --> 02:00:49,052
I will tell you something.

845
02:00:52,780 --> 02:00:55,570
Is it something bad, my Bey?

846
02:00:58,245 --> 02:01:00,605
Be patient.

847
02:01:00,978 --> 02:01:03,018
Be patient.

848
02:01:07,109 --> 02:01:09,709
What will you tell, Osman Bey?

849
02:01:13,076 --> 02:01:15,486
I will tell you something.

850
02:01:17,640 --> 02:01:19,900
When?

851
02:01:21,456 --> 02:01:26,186
When the time comes, you will see.

852
02:01:39,241 --> 02:01:43,831
If anyone wants to leave, he can.

853
02:01:48,472 --> 02:01:50,442
The way is ready.

854
02:01:51,115 --> 02:01:54,475
Whoever wants to come, can come anytime.

855
02:01:55,616 --> 02:01:57,156
Your place is ready.

856
02:01:58,485 --> 02:02:00,895
This is it.

857
02:02:19,055 --> 02:02:20,965
Can I come in, my Bey?

858
02:02:23,590 --> 02:02:25,900
Come in.

859
02:03:13,299 --> 02:03:15,519
Welcome, Priest.

860
02:03:20,462 --> 02:03:22,952
Sleep well now.

861
02:03:24,066 --> 02:03:26,596
We will talk tomorrow.

862
02:03:27,825 --> 02:03:30,205
I don't have anything to talk to you!

863
02:03:34,428 --> 02:03:39,868
Let them end my captivity.

864
02:03:55,636 --> 02:04:02,346
We won't draw a sword unless
it's for protecting you, Priest.

865
02:04:06,687 --> 02:04:13,577
If I were you, I'd pray for this captivity
to continue.

866
02:04:17,742 --> 02:04:23,492
As you won't be safe anywhere
other than here.

867
02:04:24,347 --> 02:04:26,867
Rogatus is my friend.

868
02:04:28,895 --> 02:04:32,765
He is loyal to Jesus.

869
02:04:34,335 --> 02:04:36,585
This world is a lie.

870
02:04:37,793 --> 02:04:41,063
It is, Priest.

871
02:04:43,850 --> 02:04:46,760
Now go rest.

872
02:04:49,610 --> 02:04:52,310
We will talk tomorrow.

873
02:05:15,038 --> 02:05:18,338
Is it good, my Bey?

874
02:05:18,582 --> 02:05:20,782
Yes.

875
02:05:23,789 --> 02:05:27,789
The Priest...

876
02:05:28,968 --> 02:05:31,778
chose us over them.

877
02:05:36,432 --> 02:05:42,512
He chose our shields.

878
02:05:46,722 --> 02:05:48,672
He knows that...

879
02:05:49,694 --> 02:05:52,124
the truth is with us.

880
02:05:52,487 --> 02:05:56,437
And we'll host him.

881
02:05:56,562 --> 02:05:58,422
Your command, my Bey.

882
02:05:58,493 --> 02:06:01,003
We will host him.

883
02:06:02,177 --> 02:06:03,387
Thank you.

884
02:06:05,011 --> 02:06:06,761
Thank you.

885
02:06:10,007 --> 02:06:11,647
You can leave.

886
02:06:19,515 --> 02:06:20,775
Brother.

887
02:06:22,001 --> 02:06:23,891
You stay.

888
02:06:29,948 --> 02:06:31,978
I want to tell you first.

889
02:06:41,711 --> 02:06:44,991
I have never seen a
wound like that before.

890
02:06:45,468 --> 02:06:48,488
It doesn't look like anything.

891
02:06:49,647 --> 02:06:53,897
It looks different. It's like it is
ripped off to put something in.

892
02:06:54,535 --> 02:06:57,535
To put something in...

893
02:06:57,569 --> 02:06:59,759
Kumral Abdal is skillful.

894
02:07:00,065 --> 02:07:03,715
He will cure you.
Don't worry.

895
02:07:06,650 --> 02:07:10,650
Your life is our trust.
You can rest.

896
02:07:13,647 --> 02:07:16,777
Listen to me carefully.

897
02:07:17,069 --> 02:07:20,559
Priest Gregor hides something in his tent.

898
02:07:20,808 --> 02:07:23,208
It seems important.

899
02:07:24,080 --> 02:07:26,990
So important to shed blood.

900
02:07:27,685 --> 02:07:32,475
It is inside the Bible.
Go and take it secretly.

901
02:07:36,751 --> 02:07:39,921
An replace it with this.

902
02:07:41,783 --> 02:07:45,303
- He should know who has done it.
- Your command, my Bey.

903
02:08:18,971 --> 02:08:20,901
You thought it well, brother.

904
02:08:22,220 --> 02:08:24,230
However...

905
02:08:25,390 --> 02:08:26,790
Osman...

906
02:08:27,082 --> 02:08:28,912
what is this?

907
02:08:31,986 --> 02:08:34,326
I don't know, brother.

908
02:08:35,149 --> 02:08:37,609
For now.

909
02:08:38,881 --> 02:08:41,201
However, as he comes back for it...

910
02:08:42,347 --> 02:08:45,327
and he is keeping it under his skin...

911
02:08:46,982 --> 02:08:49,502
it must be important.

912
02:08:57,822 --> 02:08:59,952
We'll see.

913
02:09:03,885 --> 02:09:07,885
He hides it inside his wound, he
comes back for it.

914
02:09:12,315 --> 02:09:15,825
It must be really important.

915
02:09:17,456 --> 02:09:20,456
If it's important for Priest...

916
02:09:21,089 --> 02:09:23,999
it sure is for the others as well.

917
02:09:26,626 --> 02:09:31,216
If it matters for the others
as well, you know...

918
02:09:34,421 --> 02:09:37,591
They may attack us.

919
02:09:38,147 --> 02:09:40,097
I know, brother.

920
02:09:40,414 --> 02:09:43,224
However, I won't give up.

921
02:09:44,157 --> 02:09:47,457
If they attack us...

922
02:09:48,004 --> 02:09:50,414
then I will bury them all...

923
02:09:50,620 --> 02:09:54,620
and I will wash their graves
with their own blood.

924
02:10:30,346 --> 02:10:35,156
Jesus Christ..

925
02:10:37,126 --> 02:10:39,946
I just wish my mind tricked me.

926
02:10:45,645 --> 02:10:49,215
I can't believe we came
back this hell again...

927
02:10:52,419 --> 02:10:54,689
With our own feet!

928
02:11:30,185 --> 02:11:34,185
What you protect is protected by us.

929
02:11:35,101 --> 02:11:37,521
Don't worry.

930
02:11:38,793 --> 02:11:40,313
Osman.

931
02:11:59,208 --> 02:12:01,108
Sir Gregor.

932
02:12:05,224 --> 02:12:07,814
We were protecting it...

933
02:12:08,179 --> 02:12:11,309
and you were almost killed
just to protect it.

934
02:12:16,709 --> 02:12:18,769
I don't understand.

935
02:12:20,964 --> 02:12:22,454
Osman...

936
02:12:25,914 --> 02:12:28,114
how can he know?

937
02:12:28,361 --> 02:12:31,091
It doesn't matter, Andreas.

938
02:12:32,714 --> 02:12:35,504
It belongs to Osman now.

939
02:12:41,020 --> 02:12:43,190
If we leave here...

940
02:12:43,690 --> 02:12:46,490
we may lose it forever.

941
02:12:52,701 --> 02:13:19,481
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com